  ($tr$В тексте сказано, что расчётливый манёвр дикого медведя (бег и прыжки на бочки) был попыткой добраться до «photographer standing on a platform four metres high» — фотографа на четырёхметровой платформе. В заметке «tried to reach a {{11}}» перефразирует «in an attempt to get to a photographer». Ответ: photographer.$tr$, $tr$The text says the wild bear's calculated manoeuvre (running and jumping on barrels) was an attempt to reach a «photographer standing on a platform four metres high». The note 'tried to reach a {{11}}' paraphrases 'in an attempt to get to a photographer'. The answer is photographer.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано, что собака и крыса полинезийцев также охотились на какапо, но сравнивается ли их опасность с опасностью самих поселенцев?$tr$, $tr$The text says Polynesian dogs and rats also hunted the kakapo, but is their danger compared with the danger of the settlers themselves?$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «...he had taken part in a highly publicized and extremely dangerous expedition to the coast of northeast Greenland». Участие в экспедиции, сопряженной со смертельным риском («extremely dangerous»), описывается выражением H (hazardous exploration — опасная исследовательская экспедиция).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «...he had taken part in a highly publicized and extremely dangerous expedition to the coast of northeast Greenland». Taking part in a life-threatening ('extremely dangerous') expedition is described by expression H (hazardous exploration).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «Great firms and great interests have had profound influence on the policies of states... played a major role in politics». Влияние на государственную политику («policies of states») означает влияние на национальные правительства — вариант A (National governments).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Great firms and great interests have had profound influence on the policies of states... played a major role in politics». Influence on state policy ('policies of states') means influence on national governments — option A (National governments).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «If just thinking about the task threatens our sense of self-worth or makes us anxious...». Мысль о задании угрожает самооценке и делает человека встревоженным. По ключу принята форма anxious.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «If just thinking about the task threatens our sense of self-worth or makes us anxious...». Just thinking about the task threatens self-worth and makes one anxious. The key accepts the form anxious.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «Their objective is to make AI technologies more trustworthy and transparent, so that organisations and individuals understand how AI decisions are made». Технологии, достойные доверия (trustworthy) и прозрачные (transparent), дают организациям и отдельным людям основание доверять решениям ИИ — из списка это confidence (F). Идея доверия к тому, как принимаются решения, не связана ни с pressure, ни с promotion, ни с остальными вариантами, поэтому F — единственный подходящий выбор.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Their objective is to make AI technologies more trustworthy and transparent, so that organisations and individuals understand how AI decisions are made». Trustworthy and transparent technologies give organisations and individuals grounds to trust AI decisions — from the list this is confidence (F). The idea of trusting how decisions are made is linked to neither pressure nor promotion nor the other options, so F is the only fitting choice.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «a short-sighted view begins to creep into working practices whereby workers learn through the ‘algorithm’s eyes’ and become dependent on its instructions». Работники становятся зависимыми (dependent) от инструкций алгоритма; существительное с этим значением — reliance (E, зависимость). Вариант confidence не подходит: речь не об уверенности работников в себе, а именно об их зависимости от предписаний алгоритма; остальные слова (pressure, promotion и т.д.) с контекстом «learn through the algorithm’s eyes» не связаны.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «a short-sighted view begins to creep into working practices whereby workers learn through the ‘algorithm’s eyes’ and become dependent on its instructions». Workers become dependent on the algorithm's instructions; the noun with this meaning is reliance (E). The confidence option doesn't fit: this is not about workers' self-confidence but their dependence on the algorithm's prescriptions; the other words (pressure, promotion, etc.) are unrelated to the 'learn through the algorithm's eyes' context.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «imported labour has been used for much large-scale production: German beet fields employed Polish workers; Mexicans and many others...». Использование ввезенной рабочей силы (поляков в Германии, мексиканцев и сицилийцев в США) означает труд приезжих рабочих — вариант H (Migrant workers).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «imported labour has been used for much large-scale production: German beet fields employed Polish workers; Mexicans and many others...». Using imported labour (Poles in Germany, Mexicans and Sicilians in the USA) means the work of migrant workers — option H (Migrant workers).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: «mental resources for skepticism physically reside in a different part of the brain than the resources used in perceiving and encoding». Физическое нахождение в разных отделах мозга («in a different part of the brain») означает размещение в различных локациях — different locations (вариант C).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «mental resources for skepticism physically reside in a different part of the brain than the resources used in perceiving and encoding». Physically residing in different parts of the brain ('in a different part of the brain') means being located in different locations — different locations (option C).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте сказано: если механизм перестройки костной ткани у белых медведей будет понят, «многие прикованные к постели люди и даже космонавты потенциально могут извлечь из этого пользу». Значит, механизм может принести пользу людям. Перефраз: «may benefit people» = «could potentially benefit». Ответ: TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: if the bone-remodelling mechanism in polar bears is understood, 'many bedridden people and even astronauts could potentially benefit'. So the mechanism may benefit people. Paraphrase: 'may benefit people' = 'could potentially benefit'. The answer is TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «50-litre capacity, with a smaller 31-litre equivalent available at a lower price». Основные 50 литров плюс 31-литровая версия — два доступных размера. Ответ — The North Face Base Camp Duffel (E).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «50-litre capacity, with a smaller 31-litre equivalent available at a lower price». The main 50 litres plus a cheaper 31-litre version — two available sizes. The answer is The North Face Base Camp Duffel (E).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «65% recycled polyester and 35% organic cotton». Переработанные и органические материалы говорят о том, что сумку создали с заботой об окружающей среде. Ответ — Fjallraven Vardag Duffel (A).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «65% recycled polyester and 35% organic cotton». Recycled and organic materials show the bag was made with care for the environment. The answer is Fjallraven Vardag Duffel (A).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «A 24-litre everyday gym bag at a reasonable price». Разумная (умеренная) цена подходит покупателю с ограниченным бюджетом. Ответ — Under Armour Sports Style Duffel (F).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «A 24-litre everyday gym bag at a reasonable price». A reasonable (moderate) price suits a budget-limited buyer. The answer is Under Armour Sports Style Duffel (F).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «A newly released lightweight outdoor bag». Формулировка «newly released» означает, что модель была недавно выпущена. Ответ — Fjallraven Vardag Duffel (A).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «A newly released lightweight outdoor bag». The wording 'newly released' means the model was recently launched. The answer is Fjallraven Vardag Duffel (A).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «A separate waterproof end compartment keeps damp equipment away from other items». Отдельное водонепроницаемое отделение изолирует сырое снаряжение от остальных вещей. Ответ — Under Armour Sports Style Duffel (F).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «A separate waterproof end compartment keeps damp equipment away from other items». A separate waterproof compartment isolates damp equipment from other items. The answer is Under Armour Sports Style Duffel (F).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «A simple gesture like this could result in a word-of-mouth recommendation to others». Устная (word-of-mouth = verbal) рекомендация — возможный итог, поэтому в пропуске «may earn a verbal …» — recommendation (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «A simple gesture like this could result in a word-of-mouth recommendation to others». A verbal (word-of-mouth) recommendation is a possible outcome, so the gap 'may earn a verbal …' takes recommendation (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «AI security remains an often overlooked topic when machine-learning systems are installed». Безопасность ИИ часто ИГНОРИРУЕТСЯ при установке систем, а не всегда учитывается. Утверждение противоречит тексту — NO.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «AI security remains an often overlooked topic when machine-learning systems are installed». AI security is often OVERLOOKED when systems are installed, not always considered. The claim contradicts the text — NO.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Aiming to win the confrontation accomplishes nothing». Стремление победить в споре ничего не даёт, поэтому в таблице «do not … the argument» — win (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Aiming to win the confrontation accomplishes nothing». Trying to win an argument achieves nothing, so the table's 'do not … the argument' takes win (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «All employers must have their own health and safety policy statement and, for businesses with more than five employees, this must be in writing». У компаний с более чем пятью сотрудниками документ о политике в сфере безопасности должен быть письменным (in writing), поэтому пропуск — statement.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «All employers must have their own health and safety policy statement and, for businesses with more than five employees, this must be in writing». Companies with more than five employees must have their safety policy document in writing, so the gap is statement.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Another will be to try to increase coral breeding rates», при этом «Coral spawn just once a year». Вторая цель — ускорить размножение кораллов. Ответ — speed up reproduction (D).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Another will be to try to increase coral breeding rates», while «Coral spawn just once a year». The second goal is to speed up coral reproduction. The answer is speed up reproduction (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Ask your builder to use a standard building contract that has been designed to comply with the Domestic Building Contracts Act, and to be fair to both client and builder». Стандартный договор создан так, чтобы соответствовать (comply with) Закону о жилищных строительных контрактах. Утверждение о соответствии стандартных договоров актуальному закону подтверждается текстом.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Ask your builder to use a standard building contract that has been designed to comply with the Domestic Building Contracts Act, and to be fair to both client and builder». The standard contract is made to comply with the Domestic Building Contracts Act. The claim that standard contracts comply with the current law is confirmed by the text.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Avoid too much writing, which may lose the reader’s interest». Избыток текста грозит потерей внимания читателя, поэтому в пропуске «risks losing the reader’s …» — interest.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Avoid too much writing, which may lose the reader’s interest». Too much text risks losing the reader's attention, so the gap 'risks losing the reader's …' takes interest.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Bring shorts to wear over the wetsuit and trainers for grip». Кроссовки нужны для сцепления, то есть это рекомендуемая обувь. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Bring shorts to wear over the wetsuit and trainers for grip». Trainers are needed for grip, i.e. this is the recommended footwear. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «But the glory days of steam cars were few». «Лучших дней было мало» = успех оказался недолгим, что соответствует утверждению A (Success was short-lived). Ловушки: про количество выпущенных машин (B) в абзаце не говорится; «непопулярными» сначала были бензиновые машины (C), а сложными в обращении они тоже были (D) — не паровые.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «But the glory days of steam cars were few». 'The glory days were few' = success was short-lived, matching claim A (Success was short-lived). Traps: nothing is said about the number of cars produced (B); it was petrol cars that were unpopular at first (C), and they were also the difficult ones to operate (D) — not steam cars.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «By 1953, 33 million US families owned a refrigerator». К 1953 году холодильники стали доступны средней семье, поэтому в пропуске «1950s: many homes had a …» — refrigerator.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «By 1953, 33 million US families owned a refrigerator». By 1953 fridges had become affordable for the average family, so the gap '1950s: many homes had a …' takes refrigerator.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «By the time the company folded in 1931, fewer than fifty of the amazing Model E steam cars had been produced». До закрытия фирмы выпустили менее пятидесяти машин, поэтому в пропуске «Fewer than … cars were produced» — 50.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «By the time the company folded in 1931, fewer than fifty of the amazing Model E steam cars had been produced». Fewer than fifty cars were produced before the firm closed, so the gap 'Fewer than … cars were produced' takes 50.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Cremation was not an Assyrian practice, suggesting the elite may have adopted local customs or may not have been Assyrian». Погребённые под дворцом могли быть не ассирийцами, а чужаками. Ответ — They suggest some governors may have been foreigners (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Cremation was not an Assyrian practice, suggesting the elite may have adopted local customs or may not have been Assyrian». Those buried beneath the palace may not have been Assyrians but outsiders. The answer is They suggest some governors may have been foreigners (B).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Display homes are usually offered by major project builders who work on a large scale and can deliver good quality and value». Демо-дома обычно предлагают крупные (major) застройщики, работающие в большом масштабе, а не малые. Утверждение приписывает это малым строителям и потому противоречит тексту.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Display homes are usually offered by major project builders who work on a large scale and can deliver good quality and value». Display homes are usually offered by large (major) builders working at scale, not small ones. The claim attributes this to small builders and therefore contradicts the text.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Egyptian laborers who either donated their time as community service or were paid for their labor». Труд на строительстве монументов был либо оплачиваемым, либо безвозмездным — «в качестве общественной службы» (community service), поэтому в пропуске «Workers contributed community … or were paid» — community service.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Egyptian laborers who either donated their time as community service or were paid for their labor». Work on building the monuments was either paid or unpaid — 'as community service' — so the gap 'Workers contributed community … or were paid' takes community service.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Even if physical remains are lost, a rich record of Tushan’s history … has been preserved in the … archives and publications». Если руины затопит, документальные записи останутся единственным источником о городе. Ответ — Documents may become the only source about Tushan (D).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Even if physical remains are lost, a rich record of Tushan’s history … has been preserved in the … archives and publications». If the ruins are flooded, documentary records will remain the only source about the city. The answer is Documents may become the only source about Tushan (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Filson Medium Rugged Twill Duffel: Premium quality, likely to last a lifetime». Высшее качество и пожизненный срок службы — признаки особой долговечности. Ответ — Filson Rugged Twill Duffel (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Filson Medium Rugged Twill Duffel: Premium quality, likely to last a lifetime». Top quality and a lifetime of service are marks of exceptional durability. The answer is Filson Rugged Twill Duffel (B).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Freelancing requires motivation and active efforts to find work». Фрилансу нужны самомотивация и активный поиск работы; без мотивации найти её трудно, поэтому в пропуске «Limited … may prevent graduates finding work» — motivation.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Freelancing requires motivation and active efforts to find work». Freelancing needs self-motivation and active job hunting; without motivation it is hard to find, so the gap 'Limited … may prevent graduates finding work' takes motivation.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Graduates often work without payment, which companies may expect». Компании могут ожидать бесплатной работы, поэтому в пропуске «work without …» — payment.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Graduates often work without payment, which companies may expect». Companies may expect unpaid work, so the gap 'work without …' takes payment.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «He also introduced the use of cellophane, the first transparent material for food packaging». Первым прозрачным упаковочным материалом стал целлофан, поэтому в пропуске «used … packaging» — cellophane.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «He also introduced the use of cellophane, the first transparent material for food packaging». Cellophane was the first transparent packaging material, so the gap 'used … packaging' takes cellophane.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «He argues that as well as outward behaviour, brain imaging is needed to show that the octopuses are replaying sequences of activities …». Шил считает необходимыми дополнительные исследования (нейровизуализацию), то есть выступает за продолжение изучения снов осьминогов. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «He argues that as well as outward behaviour, brain imaging is needed to show that the octopuses are replaying sequences of activities …». Shil considers further research (neuroimaging) necessary, i.e. he supports continuing to study octopus dreams. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «He developed quick-freezing techniques that reduced the damage that crystals caused». Быстрая заморозка уменьшила вред от кристаллов льда, образующихся в клетках продукта, поэтому в пропуске «quick freezing so … caused less damage» — crystals.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «He developed quick-freezing techniques that reduced the damage that crystals caused». Quick freezing reduced harm from ice crystals forming in the product's cells, so the gap 'quick freezing so … caused less damage' takes crystals.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «If someone wished to enter, he or she would have needed to know in advance how to find the location of the true opening in the wall». Желающему войти нужно было заранее знать, где находится настоящий вход, — location.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «If someone wished to enter, he or she would have needed to know in advance how to find the location of the true opening in the wall». Anyone wishing to enter needed to know in advance where the true entrance was — location.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «If we accept this model, it follows that streaming students with similar ZPDs would be an efficient and effective solution. And that forcing everyone on the same hike – regardless of aptitude – would be madness». Из модели Выготского следует поддержка стриминга, а смешанные классы названы безумием. Автор описывает это как довод против смешанных классов, поэтому утверждение «модель Выготского поддерживает смешанные классы» противоречит его позиции — NO.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «If we accept this model, it follows that streaming students with similar ZPDs would be an efficient and effective solution. And that forcing everyone on the same hike – regardless of aptitude – would be madness». Vygotsky's model implies support for streaming, while mixed classes are called madness. The author presents this as an argument against mixed classes, so the claim that 'Vygotsky's model supports mixed classes' contradicts his position — NO.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «If we are to reap the benefits and minimise the potential harms of AI … we need to have a discussion about AI ethics and the distrust that many people have towards machine learning». Чтобы извлечь пользу и снизить вред, нужно обсуждать недоверие и опасения людей — YES.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «If we are to reap the benefits and minimise the potential harms of AI … we need to have a discussion about AI ethics and the distrust that many people have towards machine learning». To reap the benefits and reduce harm, people's distrust and concerns must be discussed — YES.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Imported from Poland, they have spent the best part of three years in a six-acre pen». Птиц завезли из Польши, поэтому в пропуске «Birds came from …» — Poland.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Imported from Poland, they have spent the best part of three years in a six-acre pen». The birds were brought from Poland, so the gap 'Birds came from …' takes Poland.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «In 1880, a shipment of Australian beef and mutton was sent, frozen, to England». Говядина и баранина — это мясо, поэтому в пропуске «1880: first shipments were …» — meat.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «In 1880, a shipment of Australian beef and mutton was sent, frozen, to England». Beef and mutton are meat, so the gap '1880: first shipments were …' takes meat.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «In order to be engaged in the higher professions in ancient Egypt, a person had to be literate and so first had to become a scribe. The apprenticeship for this job lasted many years and was tough and challenging». Чтобы заниматься более престижными профессиями, нужно было стать писцом (scribe); обучение этой профессии длилось долгие годы («lasted many years» = «lengthy training»), поэтому ответ — scribe (A).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «In order to be engaged in the higher professions in ancient Egypt, a person had to be literate and so first had to become a scribe. The apprenticeship for this job lasted many years and was tough and challenging». To enter the higher professions one had to become a scribe; training for this job lasted many years ('lasted many years' = 'lengthy training'), so the answer is scribe (A).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Include measurable achievements». В резюме добавляют измеримые достижения, поэтому в пропуске «Include quantifiable … from previous work» — achievements.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Include measurable achievements». Measurable achievements are added to a CV, so the gap 'Include quantifiable … from previous work' takes achievements.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Less significant is the small benefit for those lucky clever students in the higher sets». Умным ученикам в сильных группах перепадает лишь малая выгода, поэтому в пропуске «Minimal benefit accrues to the …» — E (brightest pupils).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Less significant is the small benefit for those lucky clever students in the higher sets». Clever pupils in top sets get only a small benefit, so the gap 'Minimal benefit accrues to the …' takes E (brightest pupils).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Make the CV easy to read and divide it into appropriate sections». Резюме делят на подходящие разделы, поэтому в пропуске «Divide the CV into suitable …» — sections.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Make the CV easy to read and divide it into appropriate sections». A CV is divided into suitable sections, so the gap 'Divide the CV into suitable …' takes sections.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Many features make it heavier than some bags». Прямо сказано, что из-за обилия функций сумка тяжелее некоторых других. Ответ — Deuter Trans Alpine Pro (C).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Many features make it heavier than some bags». It directly says the abundance of features makes the bag heavier than some others. The answer is Deuter Trans Alpine Pro (C).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Many managers are simply not aware of their responsibilities». «Не осознают свои обязанности» = «may not know their responsibilities», поэтому пропуск — responsibilities.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Many managers are simply not aware of their responsibilities». 'Not aware of their responsibilities' = 'may not know their responsibilities', so the gap is responsibilities.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Most states have their own building authority who you can contact to check a builder’s licence». Строительные ведомства штатов (building authority) позволяют проверить (check = verify) лицензию строителя. Смысл утверждения полностью совпадает с текстом, поэтому оно верно.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Most states have their own building authority who you can contact to check a builder’s licence». States' building authorities let you verify (check = verify) a builder's licence. The claim's meaning fully matches the text, so it is correct.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «One aim will be to carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters». Поиск видов, пригодных к изменившемуся морю, — первая цель исследований. Ответ — find species suited to changed seas (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «One aim will be to carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters». Searching for species suited to the changed seas is the research's first aim. The answer is find species suited to changed seas (B).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Other advice from the Health and Safety Executive for small businesses tackles specific issues, such as helping small companies to deal with work-related stress». Ведомство консультирует малые компании по борьбе с рабочим стрессом, поэтому в пропуске «advise about work-related …» — stress.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Other advice from the Health and Safety Executive for small businesses tackles specific issues, such as helping small companies to deal with work-related stress». The agency advises small companies on coping with work stress, so the gap 'advise about work-related …' takes stress.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Other birds have already shown strong loyalty to the site». Молодая птица улетала во Францию, но вернулась к сородичам — привязанность к новому дому. В пропуске «show … to their new home» — loyalty (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Other birds have already shown strong loyalty to the site». The young bird flew to France but returned to its kin — attachment to the new home. The gap 'show … to their new home' takes loyalty (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Our muscles also twitch slightly, though they are largely paralysed». Во время REM-сна мышцы слегка подёргиваются, поэтому в пропуске «eyes and muscles move … during REM sleep» — глагол twitch (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Our muscles also twitch slightly, though they are largely paralysed». During REM sleep muscles twitch slightly, so the gap 'eyes and muscles move … during REM sleep' takes the verb twitch (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Proofread spelling, grammar and dates …». Вычитка орфографии и грамматики означает проверку текста на ошибки, поэтому в пропуске «Check for spelling and grammar …» — mistakes.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Proofread spelling, grammar and dates …». Proofreading spelling and grammar means checking the text for errors, so the gap 'Check for spelling and grammar …' takes mistakes.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «REM sleep activity was high in brain regions involved in processing visual information». У голубей активны зоны обработки зрительной информации, поэтому в пропуске «regions that process … input» — visual (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «REM sleep activity was high in brain regions involved in processing visual information». In pigeons the zones processing visual information are active, so the gap 'regions that process … input' takes visual (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Research the role and put the necessary skills near the beginning». Нужные для должности навыки ставят в начало, поэтому в пропуске «Highlight essential … for the job early in the CV» — skills.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Research the role and put the necessary skills near the beginning». The skills needed for the job go at the start, so the gap 'Highlight essential … for the job early in the CV' takes skills.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Scribes noted the everyday activities in ancient Egypt and wrote about everything from grain stocks to tax records». Писцы писали «обо всём» — от запасов зерна до налоговых записей, то есть на самые разные темы (вариант B). Ловушки: о сверхдлинном рабочем дне ничего не сказано (A); писцы были выходцами из привилегированных слоёв, а не из чернорабочих (C); египтяне, напротив, гордились своим трудом (D).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Scribes noted the everyday activities in ancient Egypt and wrote about everything from grain stocks to tax records». The scribes wrote 'about everything' — from grain stocks to tax records, i.e. on the most diverse topics (option B). Traps: nothing is said about an extra-long working day (A); scribes came from privileged strata, not labourers (C); Egyptians, on the contrary, took pride in their work (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Streaming students by diagnosed achievement automatically limits what the teacher feels the student is capable of». Распределение по потокам сужает представления учителя о возможностях ученика, то есть формирует заниженные ожидания — в пропуске «Teachers develop … of streamed students» — B (lower expectations).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Streaming students by diagnosed achievement automatically limits what the teacher feels the student is capable of». Streaming narrows the teacher's view of pupils' capabilities, i.e. forms lowered expectations — the gap 'Teachers develop … of streamed students' takes B (lower expectations).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Surfing lessons can be added». К коастерингу можно добавить уроки сёрфинга, то есть совместить его с занятием другим видом спорта. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Surfing lessons can be added». Surfing lessons can be added to coasteering, i.e. combined with another sport. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The Music Service is involved in several partnerships with schools and with music and community organisations … you will be expected to increase the number and scope of these». Менеджер должен расширять партнёрства с организациями («build partnerships»), поэтому пропуск — partnerships.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The Music Service is involved in several partnerships with schools and with music and community organisations … you will be expected to increase the number and scope of these». The manager must expand partnerships with organisations ('build partnerships'), so the gap is partnerships.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The Spanish erect poles for nests … and in Alsace householders install cartwheels for storks to build nests on their roofs». После реинтродукций в Европе места для гнездований создавали самыми разными способами (столбы у трасс, колёса на крышах) — вариант A. Ловушки: дороги не перенаправляли (не B), жильё для защиты от погоды — лишь эпизод в Болгарии, не следствие реинтродукций (не C), об укреплении крыш речи нет (не D).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The Spanish erect poles for nests … and in Alsace householders install cartwheels for storks to build nests on their roofs». After reintroductions in Europe, nesting places were created in highly diverse ways (poles by roads, wheels on roofs) — option A. Traps: roads were not redirected (not B); weather-protection housing is only a Bulgarian episode, not a consequence of reintroductions (not C); nothing is said about reinforcing roofs (not D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The apprenticeship for this job lasted many years and was tough and challenging». Речь идёт о профессии писца: обучение длилось долгие годы = «lengthy training», поэтому ответ — scribe (A).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The apprenticeship for this job lasted many years and was tough and challenging». This is about the scribe's profession: training lasted many years = 'lengthy training', so the answer is scribe (A).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The blocks were then moved into position by unskilled laborers. These people were mostly farmers who could do nothing with their land during the months when the Nile River overflowed its banks». Перевозкой блоков занимались в основном земледельцы, свободные от полевых работ в сезон разлива, поэтому в пропуске «Moving stones was often done by …» — farmers.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The blocks were then moved into position by unskilled laborers. These people were mostly farmers who could do nothing with their land during the months when the Nile River overflowed its banks». Moving blocks was mostly done by farmers free from field work in flood season, so the gap 'Moving stones was often done by …' takes farmers.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The brightest ones will never summit Mount Qomolangma». В смешанном классе самые способные «никогда не взойдут на Эверест» — их пик (высший потенциал) останется недостигнутым, что соответствует варианту C (unrealised potential). Ни о неподходящих маршрутах (A), ни об интересных заданиях (B), ни о не признанных ограничениях (D) метафора не говорит.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The brightest ones will never summit Mount Qomolangma». In a mixed class the most able 'will never climb Everest' — their peak (highest potential) stays unreached, matching option C (unrealised potential). The metaphor says nothing about unsuitable routes (A), interesting tasks (B) or unrecognised limits (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The customer needs to do this before being able to hear your solution». Клиент способен воспринять предложенное решение, лишь успокоившись, поэтому в пропуске «cannot hear a … until calm» — solution (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The customer needs to do this before being able to hear your solution». The client can take in the proposed solution only once calm, so the gap 'cannot hear a … until calm' takes solution (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The fact that they were infertile and did not hatch was not too disappointing». Яйца оказались неоплодотворёнными и не вылупились, поэтому в пропуске «the eggs were …» — infertile (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The fact that they were infertile and did not hatch was not too disappointing». The eggs were unfertilised and did not hatch, so the gap 'the eggs were …' takes infertile (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The often huge blocks were then pushed onto sleds, devices better suited than wheeled vehicles to moving weighty objects over shifting sand». Сани лучше колёсного транспорта подходили для перевозки тяжестей по зыбучему песку, поэтому пропуск — shifting sand.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The often huge blocks were then pushed onto sleds, devices better suited than wheeled vehicles to moving weighty objects over shifting sand». Sleds suited shifting sand better than wheeled transport, so the gap is shifting sand.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The practice is intuitively appealing to almost every stakeholder». Практика стриминга привлекательна почти для всех участников процесса — то есть «имеет широкий отклик» (вариант A, appeals broadly). О пользе для умных (B), простоте внедрения (C) или различиях между школами (D) в этом абзаце не говорится.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The practice is intuitively appealing to almost every stakeholder». The streaming practice appeals to almost all participants — i.e. it 'resonates broadly' (option A, appeals broadly). Nothing is said in this paragraph about benefits for the clever (B), ease of implementation (C) or differences between schools (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The reed cutter … harvested papyrus plants along the Nile, had to bear in mind that he worked in an area that was also home to wildlife that, at times, could prove fatal». Резчик тростника ежедневно работал в месте обитания смертельно опасных животных — постоянный риск (daily hazards), поэтому ответ — reed cutter (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The reed cutter … harvested papyrus plants along the Nile, had to bear in mind that he worked in an area that was also home to wildlife that, at times, could prove fatal». The reed cutter worked daily where lethally dangerous animals lived — a constant risk (daily hazards), so the answer is reed cutter (B).$tr$),
