  ($tr$В тексте: «The tablets mostly concern barley movements». Таблички касались перевозок ячменя, поэтому в пропуске «Tablets mainly recorded the transport of …» — barley.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «The £40 fee includes wetsuits, helmets and a buoyancy aid». Wetsuits, helmets and a buoyancy aid are included in the fee; only towels cost extra ('Towels can be hired'). The claim that equipment must be hired separately contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «The £40 fee includes wetsuits, helmets and a buoyancy aid». Гидрокостюмы, шлемы и спасательный жилет уже входят в плату; за отдельную плату берут только полотенца («Towels can be hired»). Утверждение о необходимости отдельно нанимать снаряжение противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «There are also ceramic discs and whistles». Ceramic items include discs and whistles, so the gap 'ceramic discs and …' takes whistles.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «There are also ceramic discs and whistles». Керамические предметы включают диски и свистки, поэтому в пропуске «ceramic discs and …» — whistles.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «There is also something exciting about passing on skills and knowledge that you yourself have just mastered – a certain pride and zeal, a certain freshness». Passing on newly mastered knowledge is described as exciting and pride-bringing, i.e. rewarding. This matches the claim — YES.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «There is also something exciting about passing on skills and knowledge that you yourself have just mastered – a certain pride and zeal, a certain freshness». Передача только что освоенных знаний описана как волнующая и приносящая гордость, то есть вознаграждающая. Это совпадает с утверждением — YES.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «These people were mostly farmers who could do nothing with their land during the months when the Nile River overflowed its banks». In the months of the Nile flood, farmers physically could not work their fields — 'unable to work at certain times' (option C, farmer).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «These people were mostly farmers who could do nothing with their land during the months when the Nile River overflowed its banks». В месяцы разлива Нила земледельцы физически не могли работать на своих полях — «не могли работать в определённые периоды» (вариант C, farmer).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «They can’t opt out of this responsibility just by putting up a sign». Dry cleaners are legally obliged to look after items, and a 'we are not responsible' sign does not release them (they aren't responsible … this isn't necessarily true). The claim is confirmed by the text — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «These students tend to have much higher representation of low socioeconomic class». Низкий социально-экономический статус — это неблагополучные слои, поэтому в пропуске «many with …» — F (disadvantaged backgrounds).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «These students tend to have much higher representation of low socioeconomic class». Low socioeconomic status means disadvantaged groups, so the gap 'many with …' takes F (disadvantaged backgrounds).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «They can’t opt out of this responsibility just by putting up a sign». Химчистка юридически обязана заботиться о вещах, и табличка «мы не отвечаем за вещи» не снимает с неё ответственность (they aren’t responsible … this isn’t necessarily true). Утверждение подтверждается текстом — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «They can’t opt out of this responsibility just by putting up a sign». Dry cleaners are legally obliged to look after items, and a 'we are not responsible' sign does not release them (they aren't responsible … this isn't necessarily true). The claim is confirmed by the text — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «This job was done by skilled stonemasons working with copper chisels and wooden mallets». Блоки обрабатывали медными зубилами, поэтому в пропуске «Blocks were shaped with … chisels» — copper.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «This job was done by skilled stonemasons working with copper chisels and wooden mallets». Blocks were shaped with copper chisels, so the gap 'Blocks were shaped with … chisels' takes copper.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «This practice was in keeping with the value of ma’at (harmony and balance) … One was expected to care for others as much as oneself and contributing to the common good was an expression of this». Принцип маат объяснял, каким должен быть вклад каждого человека в общество, то есть взгляд на социальную роль (вариант B). Об выражении верований в искусстве (A), о том, чьи мнения ценились (C), и о свободе выражения (D) текст не говорит.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «This practice was in keeping with the value of ma’at (harmony and balance) … One was expected to care for others as much as oneself and contributing to the common good was an expression of this». The maat principle explained what each person's contribution to society should be, i.e. a view of the social role (option B). The text says nothing about expressing beliefs in art (A), whose opinions were valued (C), or freedom of expression (D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «This process results in about six months of fasting, where the female bears have to keep themselves and their cubs alive, depleting their own calcium and calorie reserves». Fasting (пост — жизнь без еды) на протяжении «about six months» дословно соответствует утверждению «survive around six months without food»: самки существуют за счёт собственных запасов.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «This process results in about six months of fasting, where the female bears have to keep themselves and their cubs alive, depleting their own calcium and calorie reserves». Fasting (living without food) for 'about six months' matches the claim 'survive around six months without food' verbatim: the females survive on their own reserves.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «While teachers are traditionally the MKOs in classrooms, the value of knowledgeable student peers must not go unrecognised either». Автор утверждает ценность знающих одноклассников как MKO, но нигде не говорится, сомневаются ли какие-то учителя в том, чтобы ученики брали на себя эту роль. Информации нет — NOT GIVEN.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «While teachers are traditionally the MKOs in classrooms, the value of knowledgeable student peers must not go unrecognised either». The author affirms the value of knowledgeable classmates as MKOs, but nowhere does it say whether any teachers doubt pupils taking on this role. There is no information — NOT GIVEN.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «Wood expands as it absorbs moisture from the air». Древесина разбухает (expands), впитывая влагу из воздуха, поэтому в пропуске «… entering wood causes it to swell» — moisture (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «Wood expands as it absorbs moisture from the air». Wood swells (expands) as it absorbs moisture from the air, so the gap '… entering wood causes it to swell' takes moisture (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «World War II gave a boost to the frozen food industry because tin was being used for munitions». Жесть (олово) уходила на военные нужды, консервы нормировали, а мороженые продукты были дёшевы, поэтому в пропуске «shortage of …» — tin.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «World War II gave a boost to the frozen food industry because tin was being used for munitions». Tin went to military needs, canned goods were rationed, and frozen products were cheap, so the gap 'shortage of …' takes tin.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «You have five business days within which you may withdraw from the contract after signing it». После подписания договора у клиента есть пять рабочих дней, в течение которых он может отказаться от него (withdraw). Утверждение «от подписанного договора нельзя отказаться» прямо противоречит тексту.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «You have five business days within which you may withdraw from the contract after signing it». After signing, the client has five working days to withdraw from it. The claim that 'a signed contract cannot be cancelled' directly contradicts the text.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «a pair of white storks built an untidy nest of sticks in the top branches of a huge oak». Гнездо сложено из веточек, поэтому в пропуске «Storks put … together in a tree» — sticks (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «a pair of white storks built an untidy nest of sticks in the top branches of a huge oak». The nest is made of sticks, so the gap 'Storks put … together in a tree' takes sticks (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «a programme to broaden what is taught in school music lessons, to include instruments and musical styles from around the world, and you will be required to further develop this emphasis on diversity». В уроках музыки нужно продвигать разнообразие — инструменты и стили со всего мира, поэтому пропуск — diversity.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «a programme to broaden what is taught in school music lessons, to include instruments and musical styles from around the world, and you will be required to further develop this emphasis on diversity». Music lessons must promote diversity — instruments and styles from around the world, so the gap is diversity.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «a purchase that did not meet their expectations». Клиент купил товар или услугу, не оправдавшие его ожиданий, поэтому в пропуске «customer had … not met» — expectations (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «a purchase that did not meet their expectations». The client bought a product or service that did not meet their expectations, so the gap 'customer had … not met' takes expectations (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «adding a neural network to a system of government does not mean it will instantly become more inclusive or fair». Речь о справедливости и равенстве; из слов A–I подходит Equality. Ответ — F.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «adding a neural network to a system of government does not mean it will instantly become more inclusive or fair». This is about fairness and equality; from words A–I, Equality fits. The answer is F.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «algae that live within them, which in turn get protection». Водоросли, живя внутри кораллов, получают защиту, поэтому в пропуске «Algae gain … from living inside corals» — protection.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «algae that live within them, which in turn get protection». Algae living inside corals gain protection, so the gap 'Algae gain … from living inside corals' takes protection.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «an unmodified Doble Model E runs clean enough to pass the emissions laws in California today, and they are pretty strict». Законы Калифорнии названы «pretty strict» (довольно строгими), поэтому в пропуске «The cars satisfy California’s … emissions laws» — strict (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «an unmodified Doble Model E runs clean enough to pass the emissions laws in California today, and they are pretty strict». California's laws are called 'pretty strict', so the gap 'The cars satisfy California's … emissions laws' takes strict (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «apparently used to record goods and people entering and leaving». Жетоны служили для учёта (записи), поэтому в пропуске «used to keep … of goods and people» — существительное records.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «apparently used to record goods and people entering and leaving». The tokens served for accounting (recording), so the gap 'used to keep … of goods and people' takes the noun records.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «arguing that the huge number of regulations – not just on health and safety but also on tax, the minimum wage, and much, much more – makes their work difficult». Огромное количество норм и правил (regulations) затрудняет работу, поэтому в пропуске «They face many …» — regulations.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «arguing that the huge number of regulations – not just on health and safety but also on tax, the minimum wage, and much, much more – makes their work difficult». The huge number of norms and rules (regulations) makes work difficult, so the gap 'They face many …' takes regulations.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «bleaching events that strip reefs of their colour and eventually kill them». Тёплая вода лишает рифы окраски, поэтому в пропуске «Warm water can remove coral’s …» — colour.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «bleaching events that strip reefs of their colour and eventually kill them». Warm water strips reefs of colour, so the gap 'Warm water can remove coral's …' takes colour.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «businesses must train their employees about health and safety, and provide information to others who need to know, such as the contractors working for them». Политика безопасности должна охватывать не только работников, но и подрядчиков (contractors), которые часто выполняют самую опасную работу, поэтому пропуск — contractors.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «businesses must train their employees about health and safety, and provide information to others who need to know, such as the contractors working for them». The safety policy must cover not only employees but contractors, who often do the most dangerous work, so the gap is contractors.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «but this could be expensive (often around £100)». Заключение независимой организации платное и зачастую стоит около ста фунтов. Утверждение «отчёты бесплатны» противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «but this could be expensive (often around £100)». An independent body's report is paid for and often costs around a hundred pounds. The claim that 'reports are free' contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «check that employers are genuine before working». Прежде чем браться за работу, нужно убедиться, что работодатели настоящие, поэтому в пропуске «Check that potential clients are …» — genuine.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «check that employers are genuine before working». Before taking work, check that employers are genuine, so the gap 'Check that potential clients are …' takes genuine.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «climate change is driving architects to turn to treated timber as a possible resource». Экологические проблемы (изменение климата) побуждают именно проектировщиков зданий обратиться к дереву, поэтому в пропуске «Environmental concerns encourage … to use wood» — architects (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «climate change is driving architects to turn to treated timber as a possible resource». Environmental concerns (climate change) are driving precisely building designers to timber, so the gap 'Environmental concerns encourage … to use wood' takes architects (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «control measures are identified and put in place». План подъёма — это оценка рисков, при которой определяются меры контроля, поэтому в пропуске «Lift plans: establish …» — control measures (два слова).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «control measures are identified and put in place». A lift plan is a risk assessment in which control measures are identified, so the gap 'Lift plans: establish …' takes control measures (two words).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «courtyards paved with black-and-white pebble mosaics». Дворы были вымощены мозаикой из чёрно-белой гальки, поэтому в пропуске «The courtyards had patterned … on the floors» — mosaics.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «courtyards paved with black-and-white pebble mosaics». Courtyards were paved with black-and-white pebble mosaics, so the gap 'The courtyards had patterned … on the floors' takes mosaics.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «do not shut down their entire brain when they sleep, but only half of it, keeping the rest awake». Кит и дельфин отключают лишь половину мозга, поэтому в пропуске «keep … of their brain awake» — half (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «do not shut down their entire brain when they sleep, but only half of it, keeping the rest awake». Whales and dolphins shut down only half of their brain, so the gap 'keep … of their brain awake' takes half (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «documented instructions for tests that should be adhered to prior to using the equipment». Перед применением необходимо следовать инструкциям по проверкам (tests), поэтому в пропуске «may need …» — tests.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «documented instructions for tests that should be adhered to prior to using the equipment». Instructions for tests must be followed before use, so the gap 'may need …' takes tests.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «drove the Model B from Massachusetts to Detroit in order to seek investment … which he used to open the General Engineering Company. He and his brothers immediately began working on the Model C». Перед работой над моделью C братья привлекли инвестиции, то есть собрали капитал. Ответ — B (raised capital). Переезд в Детройт был средством для поиска инвестиций (не A), о найме работника (C) не говорится, а прежние наработки они развивали, а не отбрасывали (не D).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «drove the Model B from Massachusetts to Detroit in order to seek investment … which he used to open the General Engineering Company. He and his brothers immediately began working on the Model C». Before working on Model C the brothers raised investment, i.e. gathered capital. The answer is B (raised capital). Moving to Detroit was a means of seeking investment (not A), nothing is said about hiring a worker (not C), and they developed prior work rather than discarding it (not D).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «during REM sleep animals are more vulnerable to extremes of temperature». В REM-сне животные уязвимы к экстремальным температурам, поэтому в пропуске «sensitive to …» — temperature (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «during REM sleep animals are more vulnerable to extremes of temperature». In REM sleep animals are vulnerable to temperature extremes, so the gap 'sensitive to …' takes temperature (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «each requiring special permissions to be accessed». Для доступа нужны специальные разрешения; из слов A–I это Approval. Ответ — I.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «each requiring special permissions to be accessed». Special permissions are needed for access; from words A–I this is Approval. The answer is I.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «equipment bearing a CE mark has been constructed to international standards». Правильно сконструированное оборудование несёт знак CE, поэтому в заметке «Equipment: CE …» — mark (в сумме «CE mark», не более двух слов).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «equipment bearing a CE mark has been constructed to international standards». Properly constructed equipment bears a CE mark, so the note 'Equipment: CE …' takes mark ('CE mark' in total, no more than two words).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «flexible hours». Рабочие часы фрилансера гибкие, поэтому в пропуске «Benefit from … in working hours» — существительное flexibility.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «flexible hours». A freelancer's working hours are flexible, so the gap 'Benefit from … in working hours' takes the noun flexibility.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «had a unique means of conserving potatoes for later consumption. They froze them overnight … then dried them in the sun». Жители Анд консервировали картофель: замораживали на ночь, вытаптывали влагу и сушили на солнце. В пропуске «preserve … by freezing and drying» — potatoes.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «had a unique means of conserving potatoes for later consumption. They froze them overnight … then dried them in the sun». Andean people preserved potatoes by freezing them overnight, treading out moisture and drying them in the sun. The gap 'preserve … by freezing and drying' takes potatoes.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «has long advocated a more sensible and realistic approach». Подход Рассела назван более разумным и реалистичным — то есть практичным, а не непрактичным. Утверждение противоречит позиции автора — NO.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «has long advocated a more sensible and realistic approach». Russell's approach is called more sensible and realistic — i.e. practical, not impractical. The claim contradicts the author's position — NO.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «human experts found it hard to trust the machine». Врачи не доверяли машине, то есть сомневались в её надёжности; из слов A–I подходит Reliability. Ответ — A.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «human experts found it hard to trust the machine». Doctors did not trust the machine, i.e. doubted its reliability; from words A–I, Reliability fits. The answer is A.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «hundreds of tiny tokens representing quantities and commodities». Маленькие жетоны обозначали товары и их количество, поэтому в пропуске «Small … represented goods and quantities» — tokens.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «hundreds of tiny tokens representing quantities and commodities». Tiny tokens denoted goods and their quantities, so the gap 'Small … represented goods and quantities' takes tokens.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «inhabited by Assyrian settlers and deportees moved from across the empire». Город был заселён ассирийскими переселенцами и депортированными, то есть стоял на территории, занятой ассирийцами. Ответ — It was built in an area taken over by Assyrians (A).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «inhabited by Assyrian settlers and deportees moved from across the empire». The city was inhabited by Assyrian settlers and deportees, i.e. stood in territory taken over by Assyrians. The answer is It was built in an area taken over by Assyrians (A).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «inspectors could make employers aware of what they really need to know, rather than swamping them with mountains of leaflets which may not be relevant». «Заваливать горами листовок» (swamping with mountains of leaflets) = «overwhelm with leaflets», поэтому пропуск — leaflets.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «inspectors could make employers aware of what they really need to know, rather than swamping them with mountains of leaflets which may not be relevant». 'Swamping with mountains of leaflets' = 'overwhelm with leaflets', so the gap is leaflets.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «is another indicator of the prosperity of Mapungubwe society». Профессиональная керамика — показатель процветания общества, поэтому в пропуске «The community’s … is indicated by the amount of professionally made pottery» — prosperity.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «is another indicator of the prosperity of Mapungubwe society». Professional pottery indicates the society's prosperity, so the gap 'The community's … is indicated by the amount of professionally made pottery' takes prosperity.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «it stems from humans’ tendency to personify inanimate objects». Страх перед машинами происходит от привычки очеловечивать неживые предметы, то есть приписывать им человеческие качества. Ответ — attributing human qualities to things (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «it stems from humans’ tendency to personify inanimate objects». Fear of machines stems from the habit of personifying inanimate objects, i.e. attributing human qualities to things. The answer is attributing human qualities to things (B).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «its maximum speed was pushed to over a hundred miles per hour … with negligible emissions». Доработанная Model E достигла более ста миль в час и почти не дымила, поэтому в пропуске «A later Model E increased its … and kept emissions low» — speed (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «its maximum speed was pushed to over a hundred miles per hour … with negligible emissions». The refined Model E exceeded a hundred miles per hour and barely smoked, so the gap 'A later Model E increased its … and kept emissions low' takes speed (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «its vice-president Markus Mannstrom reports that the company is seeing increasing demand globally for building in wood, with climate change concerns the key driver». Рост интереса к дереву вызван именно экологическими проблемами (climate change concerns) — это сообщает вице-президент Stora Enso. Ответ — Markus Mannstrom (B).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «its vice-president Markus Mannstrom reports that the company is seeing increasing demand globally for building in wood, with climate change concerns the key driver». Growing interest in timber is driven by environmental concerns (climate change concerns) — reported by Stora Enso's vice-president. The answer is Markus Mannstrom (B).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «keep pitches brief and interesting». Предложения (питчи) для журналов и газет должны быть краткими и интересными, поэтому в пропуске «Keep … brief and persuasive» — pitches.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «keep pitches brief and interesting». Pitches for magazines and newspapers should be brief and interesting, so the gap 'Keep … brief and persuasive' takes pitches.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «lacks the human talent with the right technological capabilities to fully reap the benefits of machine intelligence». Не хватает людей с нужными навыками; из слов A–I подходит Skills. Ответ — C.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «lacks the human talent with the right technological capabilities to fully reap the benefits of machine intelligence». People with the needed skills are lacking; from words A–I, Skills fits. The answer is C.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «maintain a database of all music teachers, students, and instruments belonging to the Service». Преподаватели и ученики — это персонал (staff), инструменты — ресурсы (resources); для их учёта ведётся база данных, поэтому пропуск — database.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «maintain a database of all music teachers, students, and instruments belonging to the Service». Teachers and pupils are staff, instruments are resources; a database tracks them, so the gap is database.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «many managers of small businesses have an inadequate knowledge of health and safety issues». Недостаточные (inadequate) знания = «lack knowledge», поэтому пропуск — knowledge.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «many managers of small businesses have an inadequate knowledge of health and safety issues». Inadequate knowledge = 'lack knowledge', so the gap is knowledge.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «may have been used in ceremonies as offerings to ancestors». Подношения во время церемоний адресовались предкам, поэтому в пропуске «offerings to …» — ancestors.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «may have been used in ceremonies as offerings to ancestors». Ceremonial offerings were addressed to ancestors, so the gap 'offerings to …' takes ancestors.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «most injuries occur due to faults or weaknesses in these items». Именно второстепенное оснащение (цепи, стропы, скобы) чаще всего становится причиной травм, поэтому в пропуске — injuries.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «most injuries occur due to faults or weaknesses in these items». It is secondary equipment (chains, slings, hooks) that most often causes injuries, so the gap is injuries.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «must be inspected by a qualified engineer on a six-monthly basis». Краны осматривает квалифицированный инженер, поэтому в пропуске «inspected by an …» — engineer.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «must be inspected by a qualified engineer on a six-monthly basis». Cranes are inspected by a qualified engineer, so the gap 'inspected by an …' takes engineer.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «on some days marine wildlife can be seen». Морских животных можно увидеть лишь в некоторые дни — никакой гарантии нет. Утверждение о гарантированном наблюдении противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «on some days marine wildlife can be seen». Marine animals can be seen only on some days — no guarantee. The claim of guaranteed sightings contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «parliament debated putting greater effort into destroying them entirely for fear they might inspire republicanism». Страх перед республиканизмом = опасение, что аисты подтолкнут людей к свержению монархии — вариант D. Ловушки: аисты прилетали после зимы как символ надежды (не A); о «безопасных родах» текст говорит лишь как о современной открытке-символе (не B); на банкетах их подавали, но «только для богатых» не сказано (не C).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «parliament debated putting greater effort into destroying them entirely for fear they might inspire republicanism». Fear of republicanism = fear that storks might push people to overthrow the monarchy — option D. Traps: storks arrived after winter as a symbol of hope (not A); 'safe childbirth' is mentioned only as a modern card symbol (not B); they were served at banquets, but 'only for the rich' is never said (not C).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «participants are transported to Baggy Point and returned to the centre». Участников доставляют транспортом туда и обратно, а не идут пешком. Утверждение противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «participants are transported to Baggy Point and returned to the centre». Participants are transported there and back, not walking. The claim contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «polyps, with tentacles for capturing small marine creatures in the sea water». Пищу полипы захватывают щупальцами, поэтому в пропуске «Corals have … for capturing food» — tentacles.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «polyps, with tentacles for capturing small marine creatures in the sea water». Polyps catch food with tentacles, so the gap 'Corals have … for capturing food' takes tentacles.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «railroads first began putting blocks of ice in insulated rail cars to send butter from Ogdensburg … to Boston». В охлаждаемых вагонах возили масло, поэтому в пропуске «1851: … transported in ice-cooled rail cars» — butter.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «railroads first began putting blocks of ice in insulated rail cars to send butter from Ogdensburg … to Boston». Insulated cars carried butter, so the gap '1851: … transported in ice-cooled rail cars' takes butter.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «raised doubts about the stork ever having been a British bird». Сомнение было в том, что аист вообще является британской (местной, исконной) птицей — вариант C (storks were native). Ловушки: о безопасных местах гнездования (A), выживании в Британии (B) и финансировании чужих проектов (D) в этом абзаце не говорится.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «raised doubts about the stork ever having been a British bird». The doubt was whether the stork was ever a British (local, native) bird — option C (storks were native). Traps: safe nesting places (A), surviving in Britain (B) and funding foreign projects (D) are not discussed in this paragraph.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «responsibility for setting one’s workload». Фрилансер сам определяет объём своей работы, поэтому в пропуске «Decide the size of your …» — workload.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «responsibility for setting one’s workload». Freelancers set their own workload, so the gap 'Decide the size of your …' takes workload.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «served in the same segmented aluminum tray that was used by airlines». Использовалась ТА ЖЕ секционная ёмкость, что и у авиакомпаний, а не новый контейнер, разработанный Swanson. Утверждение противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «served in the same segmented aluminum tray that was used by airlines». The SAME sectional container as airlines used, not a new container developed by Swanson. The claim contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «ship owners from Boston, USA, had enormous blocks of Arctic ice towed all over the Atlantic for the purpose of food preservation». Деятельность бостонских судовладельцев описана, но о том, что они разбогатели на перевозке льда, в тексте не говорится — NOT GIVEN.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «ship owners from Boston, USA, had enormous blocks of Arctic ice towed all over the Atlantic for the purpose of food preservation». The Boston shipowners' activity is described, but nothing is said about them growing rich from carrying ice — NOT GIVEN.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «small figures of highly stylised humans with elongated bodies and short limbs». У человеческих фигурок вытянутые тела и короткие конечности, поэтому в пропуске «models of people with elongated …» — bodies.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «small figures of highly stylised humans with elongated bodies and short limbs». The human figures have elongated bodies and short limbs, so the gap 'models of people with elongated …' takes bodies.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «small jewellery items made from locally sourced copper». Из местной меди изготовили небольшие украшения, поэтому в пропуске «Small items of … made from a local metal» — jewellery.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «small jewellery items made from locally sourced copper». Small ornaments were made from local copper, so the gap 'Small items of … made from a local metal' takes jewellery.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «someone called a banksman … this person tells him or her which way to move it». Направлением перемещения груза руководит сигнальщик, поэтому в пропуске «use a … to direct crane driver» — banksman.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «someone called a banksman … this person tells him or her which way to move it». A banksman directs the load's movement, so the gap 'use a … to direct crane driver' takes banksman.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «squirted ink as though he were being attacked by a predator». Костелло вёл себя как ЖЕРТВА нападения хищника (бился, увеличивался в размерах, выпускал чернила), а не как охотник, преследующий добычу. Утверждение о «охоте» противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «squirted ink as though he were being attacked by a predator». Costello behaved like the VICTIM of a predator attack (thrashing, growing, squirting ink), not like a hunter chasing prey. The 'hunting' claim contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «streaming appears to significantly – and negatively – affect those students assigned to the lowest sets». Наибольшее (негативное) воздействие испытывают ученики самых слабых групп, поэтому в пропуске «Greatest impact is on pupils in the …» — D (bottom sets).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «streaming appears to significantly – and negatively – affect those students assigned to the lowest sets». Pupils in the weakest groups feel the greatest (negative) impact, so the gap 'Greatest impact is on pupils in the …' takes D (bottom sets).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «take a part-time job for regular income». Работа на полставки даёт регулярный доход, поэтому в пропуске «A second part-time … can provide regular income» — job.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «take a part-time job for regular income». Part-time work provides regular income, so the gap 'A second part-time … can provide regular income' takes job.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the Egyptian government was aware of how hard the people worked and so staged a number of festivals throughout the year to show gratitude and give them days off to relax». Правительство видело, как тяжело трудятся люди, и устраивало праздники «в знак благодарности» — его отношение было признательным (вариант D). Строгим (A), терпеливым (B) или небрежным (C) оно в тексте не описано.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the Egyptian government was aware of how hard the people worked and so staged a number of festivals throughout the year to show gratitude and give them days off to relax». The government saw how hard people worked and staged festivals 'as a mark of gratitude' — its attitude was grateful (option D). It is never described as strict (A), patient (B) or careless (C).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the HIA runs a state and national awards programme, with a category that recognises the level of customer service that a builder delivers». В программе наград HIA есть отдельная категория, признающая (recognises) уровень клиентского сервиса застройщика — прямое совпадение с утверждением, поэтому оно верно.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the HIA runs a state and national awards programme, with a category that recognises the level of customer service that a builder delivers». The HIA awards programme has a separate category recognising a builder's customer-service level — a direct match with the claim, so it is correct.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the area must have barriers or other means to ensure no one is allowed to walk under the load». Зона перемещения груза должна быть ограждена, поэтому в пропуске «put up …» — barriers.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the area must have barriers or other means to ensure no one is allowed to walk under the load». The load's movement zone must be fenced off, so the gap 'put up …' takes barriers.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the maximum they’re obliged to offer you is the value of the item when it was left with them, not what it would cost to replace as new». Максимум — стоимость вещи на момент сдачи, а НЕ цена новой. Утверждение «обязаны заплатить столько, чтобы купить новую» противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the maximum they’re obliged to offer you is the value of the item when it was left with them, not what it would cost to replace as new». The maximum is the item's value when handed over, NOT the price of a new one. The claim that 'they must pay enough to buy new' contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the plan should be talked over with the lifting crew». План подъёма обсуждается с бригадой, выполняющей подъём, поэтому в пропуске «discuss with lifting …» — crew (в сумме «lifting crew», два слова).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the plan should be talked over with the lifting crew». The lift plan is discussed with the crew performing the lift, so the gap 'discuss with lifting …' takes crew ('lifting crew' in total, two words).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the public sector typically does not have the appropriate data infrastructure to support advanced machine learning». Отсутствует инфраструктура данных; из слов A–I подходит Framework (каркас/структура). Ответ — G.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the public sector typically does not have the appropriate data infrastructure to support advanced machine learning». Data infrastructure is missing; from words A–I, Framework fits. The answer is G.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the size of a budget or number of locations». Среди подтверждающих цифр назван размер бюджета, поэтому в пропуске «the size of the … you control» — budget.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the size of a budget or number of locations». Budget size is named among the confirming figures, so the gap 'the size of the … you control' takes budget.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «the truth is that we do not know if there is an internal experience of chasing rabbits that comes along with that». Мы НЕ знаем, что происходит во внутреннем опыте спящей собаки, поэтому определить, какой у неё сейчас сон, невозможно. Утверждение противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «the truth is that we do not know if there is an internal experience of chasing rabbits that comes along with that». We do NOT know what happens in a sleeping dog's inner experience, so it is impossible to tell what dream it is having now. The claim contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «there is limited empirical evidence to suggest that streaming results in better outcomes for students». Лучшие результаты — это более высокие достижения, поэтому в пропуске «Little evidence streaming leads to …» подходит H (higher achievements).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «there is limited empirical evidence to suggest that streaming results in better outcomes for students». Better outcomes means higher achievements, so the gap 'Little evidence streaming leads to …' takes H (higher achievements).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «they fail to realize the complexity around deploying advanced machine-learning systems in the real world». Политики не понимают сложность внедрения — то есть не осознают трудности реализации национальных ИИ-инициатив. Ответ — Be unaware of the challenges of implementing national AI initiatives (C).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «they fail to realize the complexity around deploying advanced machine-learning systems in the real world». Politicians don't grasp the complexity of deployment — i.e. they are unaware of the difficulties of implementing national AI initiatives. The answer is Be unaware of the challenges of implementing national AI initiatives (C).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «they may only experience non-REM dreams, which are less vivid». Сны без REM-фазы менее яркие, поэтому в пропуске «their dreams are probably not very …» — vivid (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «they may only experience non-REM dreams, which are less vivid». Non-REM dreams are less vivid, so the gap 'their dreams are probably not very …' takes vivid (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «this spoilt the flavor and texture of the food». Кристаллы льда разрывали клетки и портили вкус и текстуру, то есть австралийский способ заморозки влиял на вкус. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «this spoilt the flavor and texture of the food». Ice crystals tore cells and spoiled flavour and texture, i.e. the Australian freezing method affected taste. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «we need the many to flourish – not suffer at the expense of a few bright stars». Автор настаивает, что приоритет — расцвет большинства, а не нескольких самых успешных. Утверждение «высших достижений нужно отдавать приоритет» прямо противоречит его взглядам — NO.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «we need the many to flourish – not suffer at the expense of a few bright stars». The author insists the priority is the flourishing of the many, not a few bright stars. The claim that 'top achievements should be prioritised' directly contradicts his views — NO.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «we will never be able to experience any animal’s dreams. That goes for other humans’ dreams too». Чужие сны, в том числе сны других людей, недоступны НАВСЕГДА, а не «скоро». Утверждение противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «we will never be able to experience any animal’s dreams. That goes for other humans’ dreams too». Others' dreams, including other people's dreams, are NEVER accessible, not 'soon'. The claim contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «went to Labrador in Canada to trap and trade furs. While he was there, he became fascinated with how the Inuit would quickly freeze fish». Бёрдсай поехал торговать пушниной, а способ инуитов увидел уже на месте. Утверждение, что он ехал специально ради этого метода, противоречит тексту — FALSE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «went to Labrador in Canada to trap and trade furs. While he was there, he became fascinated with how the Inuit would quickly freeze fish». Birdseye went to trade furs, and saw the Inuit method only once there. The claim that he travelled specifically for this method contradicts the text — FALSE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «when events are replayed in dreams, this helps to integrate memories into longer-term storage». Проигрывание событий во сне переводит воспоминания в долговременное хранилище, то есть создаёт стойкие воспоминания. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «when events are replayed in dreams, this helps to integrate memories into longer-term storage». Replaying events in dreams moves memories into long-term storage, i.e. creates lasting memories. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «with the help of a clever name and a huge advertising budget, it launched the first ‘TV Dinner’». Запуск сопровождался огромным рекламным бюджетом, то есть компания много тратила на продвижение. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «with the help of a clever name and a huge advertising budget, it launched the first ‘TV Dinner’». The launch came with a huge advertising budget, i.e. the company spent heavily on promotion. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «wooden buildings can be constructed at a greater speed than ones of concrete and steel». Деревянные здания строятся быстрее, поэтому в пропуске «Wooden buildings offer greater … of construction» — speed (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «wooden buildings can be constructed at a greater speed than ones of concrete and steel». Wooden buildings are built faster, so the gap 'Wooden buildings offer greater … of construction' takes speed (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «workers learn through the ‘algorithm’s eyes’ and become dependent on its instructions». Dependent (зависимый) → существительное со значением зависимости. В списке вариантов есть reliance (E): сочетание «growing reliance on AI recommendations» точно передаёт растущую зависимость от рекомендаций ИИ.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «workers learn through the ‘algorithm’s eyes’ and become dependent on its instructions». Dependent → the noun meaning dependence. The options list has reliance (E): the phrase 'growing reliance on AI recommendations' exactly conveys growing dependence on AI recommendations.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «you can pass your complaint to them and they may be able to help you». Профессиональная ассоциация (trade association) может помочь с жалобой — утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «you can pass your complaint to them and they may be able to help you». A professional association (trade association) may help with a complaint — the claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «you have up to six years». Обратиться в суд можно в течение шести лет с момента сдачи вещи в химчистку, поэтому обращение через девять месяцев (в пределах срока) возможно. Утверждение подтверждается — TRUE.$tr$, $tr$The text says: «you have up to six years». You can go to court within six years of handing an item to the dry cleaner, so applying after nine months (within the limit) is possible. The claim is confirmed — TRUE.$tr$),
  ($tr$В тексте: «you should know what you can and cannot do within the policy of the business you work for». Действовать нужно в рамках политики компании, поэтому в пропуске «know company …» — policy (одно слово).$tr$, $tr$The text says: «you should know what you can and cannot do within the policy of the business you work for». Act within the company's policy, so the gap 'know company …' takes policy (one word).$tr$),
  ($tr$В телеком-компании: «Pachidi and colleagues even observed people developing strategies to make the algorithm work to their own advantage. ‘We are seeing cases where workers feed the algorithm with false data to reach their targets’». Сотрудники скармливали алгоритму ложные данные ради своих показателей — это манипуляция результатами ИИ (C). Ни несогласия (A), ни раздражения от вторжения ИИ (B) в тексте нет; вариант D противоречит смыслу: работники не перекладывали задачи на ИИ, а искажали его входные данные.$tr$, $tr$At the telecom company: «Pachidi and colleagues even observed people developing strategies to make the algorithm work to their own advantage. ‘We are seeing cases where workers feed the algorithm with false data to reach their targets’». Employees fed the algorithm false data for their metrics — this is manipulating AI results (C). Neither disagreement (A) nor irritation at AI intrusion (B) is in the text; option D contradicts the sense: workers did not offload tasks onto AI but distorted its input data.$tr$),
